---
import GameLayout from "../../../layouts/GameLayout.astro";
---

<GameLayout
    title="OverTheWire: Blacksun Reading Material"
    gameName="blacksun"
    level="reading-material"
>
    <h2
        class="text-[24pt] font-normal text-[#999] mt-6 mb-4 border-b border-[#CCC] pb-2"
    >
        Reading material
    </h2>

    <p class="leading-[24px] mb-4">
        Below is a list of overall reading material which you may wish to read
        over before starting.
    </p>

    <h3 class="text-[18pt] font-normal text-[#999] mt-6 mb-2">
        Bug class exploitation
    </h3>

    <h4 class="text-[14pt] font-bold mt-4 mb-2">Format strings:</h4>

    <ul class="list-disc list-inside pl-4 leading-[24px] mb-4">
        <li>
            <a
                href="papers/formatstring-1.2.tar.gz"
                class="text-[#999] hover:text-[#CCC] no-underline"
                >Scut's formatstring paper</a
            > (class paper and recommended reading)
        </li>
        <li>
            <a
                href="papers/p59-0x07.txt"
                class="text-[#999] hover:text-[#CCC] no-underline"
                >Advances in format string exploitation</a>
        </li>
        <li>
            <a
                href="papers/format-bug-analysis.pdf"
                class="text-[#999] hover:text-[#CCC] no-underline"
                >Format bug analysis</a>
        </li>
        <li>
            <a
                href="papers/core_format_strings.pdf"
                class="text-[#999] hover:text-[#CCC] no-underline"
                >Vulnerabilities in your code - Format Strings</a>
        </li>
        <li>
            <a
                href="papers/rebel-formatstring.txt"
                class="text-[#999] hover:text-[#CCC] no-underline"
                >The Mystery of Format String Exploitation</a>
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h4 class="text-[14pt] font-bold mt-4 mb-2">Heap exploitation</h4>

    <ul class="list-disc list-inside pl-4 leading-[24px] mb-4">
        <li>
            <a
                href="papers/p57-0x09"
                class="text-[#999] hover:text-[#CCC] no-underline"
                >Once upon a free()</a
            > - Historical document, later glibc's have additional checking
        </li>
        <li>
            <a
                href="papers/p57-0x08"
                class="text-[#999] hover:text-[#CCC] no-underline"
                >Vudo - An object superstitiously believed to embody magical
                powers</a
            > - ""
        </li>
        <li>
            <a
                href="papers/p61-0x06_Advanced_malloc_exploits.txt"
                class="text-[#999] hover:text-[#CCC] no-underline"
                >Advanced Doug lea's malloc exploits</a
            > - ""
        </li>
        <li>
            <a
                href="papers/MallocMaleficarum.txt"
                class="text-[#999] hover:text-[#CCC] no-underline"
                >Malloc Maleficarum</a
            > - Recent glibc malloc exploitation document, should be relevant for
            blacksun
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h4 class="text-[14pt] font-bold mt-4 mb-2">Frame pointer overwrites</h4>

    <ul class="list-disc list-inside pl-4 leading-[24px] mb-4">
        <li>
            <a
                href="papers/P55-08"
                class="text-[#999] hover:text-[#CCC] no-underline"
                >Framepointer overwrites</a>
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h4 class="text-[14pt] font-bold mt-4 mb-2">
        Adress space layout randomisation (ASLR)/ PaX specific
    </h4>

    <ul class="list-disc list-inside pl-4 leading-[24px] mb-4">
        <li>
            <a
                href="papers/p59-0x09.txt"
                class="text-[#999] hover:text-[#CCC] no-underline"
                >Bypassing PaX ASLR protection</a
            > - somewhat outdated.
        </li>
        <li>
            <a
                href="papers/p58-0x04"
                class="text-[#999] hover:text-[#CCC] no-underline"
                >The advanced return-into-lib(c) exploits: PaX case study</a
            > - ""
        </li>
        <li>
            <a
                href="http://pax.grsecurity.net/docs/"
                class="text-[#999] hover:text-[#CCC] no-underline"
                >PaX documentation</a
            > - external link
        </li>
        <li>
            <a
                href="papers/smash_the_stack_advanced_bufferoverflow_methods.txt"
                class="text-[#999] hover:text-[#CCC] no-underline"
                >Smash the stack - Advanced bufferoverflow methods</a>
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h4 class="text-[14pt] font-bold mt-4 mb-2">Execshield documents</h4>

    <ul class="list-disc list-inside pl-4 leading-[24px] mb-4">
        <li>
            <a
                href="http://www.hackinthebox.org/print.php?sid=15604"
                class="text-[#999] hover:text-[#CCC] no-underline"
                >A Solution To Red Hat PIE Protection</a
            > - External link
        </li>
        <li>
            <a
                href="http://neworder.box.sk/newsread.php?newsid=13007"
                class="text-[#999] hover:text-[#CCC] no-underline"
                >How to Exploit Overflow Vulnerability Under Fedora Core</a
            > - External link
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h4 class="text-[14pt] font-bold mt-4 mb-2">
        Stackguard / Stack smashing protection
    </h4>

    <ul class="list-disc list-inside pl-4 leading-[24px] mb-4">
        <li>
            <a
                href="http://www.research.ibm.com/trl/projects/security/ssp/"
                class="text-[#999] hover:text-[#CCC] no-underline"
                >Stack Smashing Protection homepage</a
            > - external link
        </li>
        <li>
            <a
                href="papers/p56-0x05"
                class="text-[#999] hover:text-[#CCC] no-underline"
                >Bypassing StackGuard and StackShield</a>
        </li>
        <li>
            <a
                href="papers/StackguardPaper.pdf"
                class="text-[#999] hover:text-[#CCC] no-underline"
                >Four different tricks to bypass StackShield and StackGuard
                protection</a>
        </li>
        <li>
            <a
                href="papers/alexander0506.pdf"
                class="text-[#999] hover:text-[#CCC] no-underline"
                >Defeating compiler-level buffer overflow protection</a>
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h4 class="text-[14pt] font-bold mt-4 mb-2">
        Hardware protection (e.g amd64 / nx bit)
    </h4>

    <ul class="list-disc list-inside pl-4 leading-[24px] mb-4">
        <li>
            <a
                href="papers/no-nx.pdf"
                class="text-[#999] hover:text-[#CCC] no-underline"
                >x86-64 buffer overflow exploits and the borrowed chunks
                exploitation technique</a>
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h3 class="text-[18pt] font-normal text-[#999] mt-6 mb-2">
        Generalised papers / notes / presentations (not always indepth)
    </h3>

    <ul class="list-disc list-inside pl-4 leading-[24px] mb-4">
        <li>
            <a
                href="papers/Buffer_Overflow_Prevention.ppt"
                class="text-[#999] hover:text-[#CCC] no-underline"
                >A Comparison of Buffer Overflow Prevention Implementations and
                Their Weaknesses</a>
        </li>
        <li>
            <a
                href="papers/PaX-presentation.ppt"
                class="text-[#999] hover:text-[#CCC] no-underline"
                >Spender's PaX Presentation</a>
        </li>
        <li>
            <a
                href="papers/smashing.sxi"
                class="text-[#999] hover:text-[#CCC] no-underline"
                >Taking the fun out of smashing the stack</a>
        </li>
        <li>
            <a
                href="papers/practical_unix_security.pdf"
                class="text-[#999] hover:text-[#CCC] no-underline"
                >Practical Unix Security</a>
        </li>
        <li>
            <a
                href="papers/PaX_Memory_Protection.pdf"
                class="text-[#999] hover:text-[#CCC] no-underline"
                >PaX Memory Protection</a
            > - Linux Journal entry
        </li>
        <li>
            <a
                href="papers/advancesinsoftwareattacks.pdf"
                class="text-[#999] hover:text-[#CCC] no-underline"
                >Advances In Software Attack</a>
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h3 class="text-[18pt] font-normal text-[#999] mt-6 mb-2">
        Secure computing
    </h3>

    <ul class="list-disc list-inside pl-4 leading-[24px] mb-4">
        <li>
            <a
                href="http://kerneltrap.org/node/4005"
                class="text-[#999] hover:text-[#CCC] no-underline"
                >Seccomp announcement</a
            > - Secure Computing (seccomp) patch announcement (external link)
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h3 class="text-[18pt] font-normal text-[#999] mt-6 mb-2">
        Got some good additional papers?
    </h3>

    <p class="leading-[24px] mb-4">
        If you have some relevant papers that would be suitable for this site,
        please drop <a
            href="mailto:andrewg@felinemenace.org"
            class="text-[#999] hover:text-[#CCC] no-underline">me</a
        > an email.
    </p>
</GameLayout>
